Currently alfe has options:

--clautolisp
--briscad
--autocad

and it will run an executable it finds with some heuristic or hardwired path.

This is insuficient.

Users may have several versions of their CAD application installed and
may want to use/test one or the other explicitely.

In the case of autocad, we're using accoreconsole (notably in --mode
batch), but we might want to use also acad (the GUI autocad), notably
when we will be testing GUI aspects.


Therefore, we need:

- a way to scan and list all the CAD available.
- a way to denote them to select them easily.
- and of course, to use default to make naming easy.

* Scanning for CADs

Scanning should depend on the OS.

** MacOS

On macOS, search in /Applications
Perhaps something like: 

To find the .app bundle:

#+begin_src bash
find /Applications/ -maxdepth 3 \( -iname AutoCAD\ 20\*.app -o -iname BricsCAD\*.app \)
#+end_src

To find the application executable

#+begin_src bash
{
  find /Applications/ -maxdepth 3 -iname AutoCAD\ 20\*.app \
  | while read apppath ; do echo "${apppath}/Contents/MacOS/AutoCAD" ; done
  find /Applications/ -maxdepth 3 -iname BricsCAD\ \*.app \
  | while read apppath ; do echo "${apppath}/Contents/MacOS/bricscad" ; done
}
#+end_src

/Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2026/AutoCAD 2026.app/Contents/MacOS/AutoCAD
/Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/AutoCAD 2027.app/Contents/MacOS/AutoCAD
/Applications/BricsCAD V26.app/Contents/MacOS/bricscad


To find other tools, such as AcCoreConsole:

#+begin_src bash
{
  find /Applications/ -maxdepth 3 -iname AutoCAD\ 20\*.app \
  | while read apppath ; do echo "${apppath}/Contents/Helpers/AcCoreConsole.app/Contents/MacOS/AcCoreConsole" ; done
}
#+end_src

/Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2026/AutoCAD 2026.app/Contents/Helpers/AcCoreConsole.app/Contents/MacOS/AcCoreConsole
/Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/AutoCAD 2027.app/Contents/Helpers/AcCoreConsole.app/Contents/MacOS/AcCoreConsole



To find other executables in BricsCAD:

#+begin_src bash
find '/Applications/BricsCAD V26.app/Contents/MacOS/' -depth 1 \( -name \*.\* -o -print \)|sort 
#+end_src

** MS-Windows

Similarly, on MS-Windows. I'll let you find the native commands (with
powershell) to find CAD .exe in "C:\Program Files".

#+begin_src pwsh
"C:/Program Files/Bricsys/BricsCAD*/bricscad.exe"
#+end_src

"C:/Program Files/Bricsys/BricsCAD V25 fr_FR/bricscad.exe"

#+begin_src pwsh
"C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD*/acad.exe"
"C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD*/accoreconsole.exe"
#+end_src

"C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2022/acad.exe"
"C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2022/accoreconsole.exe"

** Linux

On Linux, AutoCAD is not availble, BricsCAD is available, but I don't know how it's installed.

clautolisp is usually installed in =/opt/local/bin/clautolisp= but anything goes, it's unix.
Let's expect it on the PATH or in the same directory as the alfe executable itself
(and IIRC, alfe doesn't fork clautolisp, it just includes it as a library, so the question is moot).

* Denotation

- =autocad= denotes the latest version of AutoCAD
- =bricscad= denotes the latest version of BricsCAD

- =autocad-2022= denotes "AutoCAD 2022/acad.exe"
- =bricscad-v25= denotes "BricsCAD V25 fr_FR/briscad.exe"
- =bricscad-v25-fr_FR= denotes "BricsCAD V25 fr_FR/briscad.exe"

I think we need to be able to select acad or accoreconsole explicitely:

- =acad= denotes the latest version of "acad.exe"
- =acad-2022= denotes "AutoCAD 2022/acad.exe"
- =accoreconsole= denotes the latest version of "acoreconsole.exe"
- =accoreconsole-2022= denotes "AutoCAD 2022/acoreconsole.exe"

Then =autocad= and =autocad-2022=, etc, will denote acad or
accoreconsole depending on the other options, in particular the
=--mode=:
- =--mode= =batch= -> =accoreconsole=
- =--mode= =automation= -> =acad=

Note: the mode selects a protocol between alfe and the cad, so any
combination is possible theorically.  If accoreconsole responds to
=COM= messages, or AppleScript messages, it can also be used with
=--mode= =automation=.


How do we select the language_contry if there are several bricscad
installed of different localisations?

On macOS or Linux, we can use LANG/LC_* to select one

On macOS, we have languages preferences. Find which domain is the most indicated,
I guess ".GlobalPreferences_m" or "Apple Global Domain".

We can make an intersection of the prefered languages with the
available languages and choose the most prefered one. Or else the first found.

#+begin_src bash :results raw
  echo all prefered languages:
  defaults read ".GlobalPreferences_m" "AppleLanguages"
  echo most prefered language:
  defaults read ".GlobalPreferences_m" "AppleLanguages"|sed -n -e '/"/{p;q;}'
#+end_src

#+RESULTS:
all prefered languages:
(
    "en-FR",
    "en-GB",
    "fr-FR"
)
most prefered language:
    "en-FR",

Perhaps something similar can be done on MS-Windows.

* New alfe option: =--list-cad-programs=

=alfe= will need an option to list the available cad and their denotation:

#+begin_src bash
alfe --list-cad-programs
#+end_src

#+begin_example
acad-2026          /Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2026/AutoCAD 2026.app/Contents/MacOS/AutoCAD
acad-2027          /Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/AutoCAD 2027.app/Contents/MacOS/AutoCAD
acad               acad-2027
accoreconsole-2026 /Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2026/AutoCAD 2026.app/Contents/Helpers/AcCoreConsole.app/Contents/MacOS/AcCoreConsole
accoreconsole-2027 /Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/AutoCAD 2027.app/Contents/Helpers/AcCoreConsole.app/Contents/MacOS/AcCoreConsole
acoreconsole       acoreconsole-2027
autocad-2026       acad-2026 or acoreconsole-2026
autocad-2027       acad-2027 or acoreconsole-2027
autocad            acad or acoreconsole
briscad-v26        /Applications/BricsCAD V26.app/Contents/MacOS/bricscad
bricscad           bricscad-v26
clautolisp-1.6.17  /opt/local/bin/clautolisp or alfe since it's embedded?
clautolisp         clautolisp-1.6.17
#+end_example

* Status

** DONE 2026-07-29 (clautolisp 1.6.22 / alfe 1.6.20) — increment 1: model + scan + list
- =cad-program= struct (kind / version / locale / path / denotation) +
  path parsers in =AFE/source/backend-cad-common.lisp=:
  =%find-autocad-year= (bare 20NN), =%find-bricscad-version= (V-token,
  "V26x64"→"V26"), =%find-locale= (ll_CC), =%cad-denotation=,
  =%cad-program-from-path=. Denotations: =acad-2026=, =accoreconsole-2022=,
  =bricscad-v26=, =bricscad-v25-fr_FR=, =clautolisp=.
- =discover-cad-programs= enumerates ALL installed CADs per OS (macOS
  /Applications globs incl. AutoCAD Helpers/AcCoreConsole; Windows Program
  Files globs; Linux /opt/bricsys), dedups by path, always includes the
  embedded clautolisp. (Unlike the per-backend =discover-*-binary= which
  return only the best one.)
- =alfe --list-cad-programs= prints =denotation  path=, one per line, then
  exits (short-circuit like =--list-encodings=; help text added). Verified on
  Linux (prints =clautolisp (embedded in alfe)=). Unit test
  =cad-program-denotation-parsing= (12 checks; suite 364/364).

** DONE 2026-07-29 (clautolisp 1.6.23 / alfe 1.6.21) — increment 2: selection
- =--cad DENOTATION= (option + =cli-options-cad= slot). Resolved in RUN (not
  at parse time) so =--mode= is known. =resolve-cad-denotation= (cad-common)
  handles exact, segment-prefix bare/partial (latest version wins), and the
  virtual =autocad[-VER]= → =acad=/=accoreconsole= per =--mode= (batch →
  accoreconsole, else acad). Case-insensitive.
- =apply-cad-selection= (cli): sets the backend (via =%set-backend-checked=,
  so =--cad= + a conflicting =--autocad/--bricscad= is a usage error) and
  points the backend's discovery at the chosen exe by exporting its
  =$*_EXE= — =AUTOCAD_EXE= / =AUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE= / =BRICSCAD_EXE= — which
  every =DETECT= already prefers; no backend code changed. accoreconsole/acad
  also default =--mode= (batch/automation) when the user left it =:auto=.
- Unknown denotation → =cli-usage-error= pointing at =--list-cad-programs=.
  Help text added. Verified: =--cad clautolisp= → CLAUTOLISP; =--cad acad-2022=
  on Linux → clean "unknown CAD program" error; =--bricscad --cad clautolisp=
  → conflict error. Unit test =cad-denotation-resolution= (11 checks; suite
  375/375).

** DONE 2026-07-29 (clautolisp 1.6.24 / alfe 1.6.22) — increment 3: locale + list-situations + docs
- Locale PREFERENCE: =resolve-cad-denotation= now breaks same-version ties by
  the host's locale preference (=%host-preferred-locales= — macOS
  =AppleLanguages= via =defaults=, then =LC_ALL=/=LC_CTYPE=/=LANG=), with
  =:preferred-locales= injectable for tests. Version still beats locale; no
  preference keeps discovery order. Test =cad-denotation-locale-preference=.
- =--list-situations= prints the six situations + directions + one-line notes
  (=print-situations= on the shared =*encoding-situations*= registry); wired
  in BOTH alfe and the clautolisp binary. Help text added.
- DOCS: alfe user-manual "Selecting a specific CAD install" (=--cad=
  denotation grammar + =--list-cad-programs= + locale tie-break) and the
  =--list-situations= mention in Encoding.
- Full suite 382/382; both binaries build and run =--list-situations= /
  =--list-cad-programs= / =--cad=.

The backend-selection feature is functionally COMPLETE. Optional later: a
per-backend =--list-situations= that resolves each situation's default +
settability against the SELECTED backend (needs the §7 provenance table in
code), and adding the new options to the formal autolisp-cli-specifications.org.

